---
description: CE + Sol/Luna engineering lifecycle
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the canonical policy at `policy/engineering-lifecycle.md`. Classify work
before execution and use the smallest safe lane: Observe and Small may be
Sol-only; Standard selects a bounded maker and independent reviewer; High-risk
uses full boundaries with only named-risk specialists. Tier 3 always wins.

Sol owns intent, planning, architecture, security, integration, synthesis,
verification, and engineering acceptance. Whenever a worker is selected, use
exact scope and observable criteria. Required review is independent,
stable-target, and read-only. Architecture and specialist quality practices are
trigger-based lenses rather than universal nested workflows.

Direct engagement is the default. In a mediated infrastructure engagement,
keep repository engineering inside one engineering root and leave live
approval, credentials, service control, deployment, rollback, live verification,
and operational acceptance with the operational controller. Nested engineering
agents must not SSH, deploy, control services, access production credentials or
state, or live-verify. Tool capability does not grant authority.

Track inspect, design, implementation, review, commit, push or pull request,
release, deployment or rollback, credentials, and production authority
separately. For substantive instrumented work, attach only allowlisted evidence
from the canonical assessment policy; unavailable host controls remain
unverified. Cursor rules preserve behavioral invariants but do not claim Codex
named-agent routing, model selection, sandbox, or approval guarantees.
